<Base title="Surface cleaner fittings" description="Most consumer surface cleaners use a 1/4 inch quick-connect inlet. Confirm PSI and GPM as well as the plug size." path="/surface-cleaner/">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Surface cleaner</p>
    <h1>Surface-cleaner fittings</h1>
    <Answer>
      The inlet is usually 1/4″ QC on homeowner decks. If your wand is M22, you need a QC wand or an adapter — the deck cleaner is not “the wrong brand.”
    </Answer>
    <p>Also match:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>PSI rating ≥ machine.</li>
      <li>GPM high enough to spin the arms. A 1.2 GPM electric on a 20 in head will sit there and sulk. That is not a fitting leak.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some pro heads use 3/8″ QC. Compare the plug to a nozzle tip before you force it into a 1/4″ wand socket.</p>
    <p><a href="/qc-14/">1/4″ QC</a> · <a href="/wand/">Wands</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
